        "tagline": "Mandatory Implementation Spec & Finisher-First WIP discipline before coding dispatch",
        "description": "Enforces Adrian's Finisher-First 70%->100% rule and complete ISA/DoD checklists prior to FirstMate-adi0 execution.",
        "categories": [
          "governance",
          "planning"
        ],
        "markdown": "# ISA & Finisher-First (`70% -> 100%`) Gate\n\n## Purpose\nPrevent half-finished 70% epics (TELOS Challenge `C0`/`C4`) and ambiguous coding handoffs across the 6 Cyber-Sec / Pentforge organizations.\n\n## Mandatory Pre-Dispatch Checklist (ISA / DoD)\nBefore assigning or escalating any repository change to `FirstMate-adi0`:\n1. **Finisher-First Check**: Confirm active commercial WIP does not exceed 3 concurrent epics and prioritize closing existing 70% work over starting net-new builds.\n2. ** Vault & Control-Plane Context**: Query `memory-query` (`--safe`) and `paperclip-ops` so prior ADRs, regressions, and open issues are accounted for.\n3. **Explicit Scope Boundary**: State exact target repository (`adi0`), in-scope files/modules, and explicit out-of-scope items.\n4. **TDD & Verification Bar**: Specify unit, integration, and E2E acceptance criteria (`>=80%` test coverage + `no-mistakes` verification).\n5. **Captain Decision Card Rule**: If human judgment is required, present **one** concise decision card at a time with recommended option first, cost/risk impact, and rollback plan.\n"
      },
      {
        "slug": "adi0-dispatch-protocol",
        "name": "adi0 FirstMate Coding Dispatch Protocol",
        "tagline": "Strict control-plane vs adi0 execution separation and PR verification contract",
        "description": "Defines how Paperclip Hermes coordinators hand off repository work to FirstMate-adi0 while keeping VPS nodes non-coding.",
        "categories": [
          "architecture",
          "execution"
        ],
        "markdown": "# `adi0` FirstMate Coding Dispatch Protocol\n\n## Core Invariant\nAll repository checkouts, code edits, builds, test runs, and git operations execute **exclusively on `adi0`** (`Mac Studio M3 Ultra`) via `FirstMate-adi0`. VPS hosts (`adi4`, `adi5`) operate strictly as orchestration, scouting, observability, and review control planes.\n\n## Handoff Steps\n1. Attach project, active Company/Team Goal, and complete ISA specification to the Paperclip issue.\n2. Verify custody & harness rules:\n   - `ReviewForge` (`P-OCD-70`): private `adibirzu/reviewforge` on `adi0` only; zero overlap with employer IP.\n   - `AetherOps`: `grok`, `codex`, `claude` harnesses allowed; `agy` and `cursor` blocked.\n   - `pentforge-rai-policy`: strict separation between Pentforge security products and RAI Accounting.\n3. Delegate implementation to `FirstMate-adi0` and review returned PR evidence (test output, coverage >=80%, security scan, deployment health).\n"
      }
